          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Run a quick PCA analysis on the depth profiling feature data. The file is at:\n/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_3/projects/gen-depth-fingerprint/artifacts/_project/supplement/data/features_all_models.csv\n\nThis CSV has 37,058 rows with columns: model_name, seed_id, depth, and 7 features (entropy_mean, entropy_std, entropy_max, entropy_min, tail_decay, ttr, hapax_ratio).\n\nTasks:\n1. Read the CSV and extract just the 7 feature columns\n2. Standardize features (z-score)\n3. Run PCA on all 7 features\n4. Report: explained variance ratio for each component (PC1 through PC7)\n5. Report: loadings (component weights) for PC1 and PC2\n6. Specifically analyze: if you subset to just the 3 \"drifting\" features (entropy_mean, ttr, hapax_ratio), what fraction of their variance is explained by a single PC?\n7. Also compute: correlation matrix of all 7 features (just the upper triangle)\n\nFormat output as clean numbers I can cite in a paper. Use Python with sklearn/numpy/pandas."
            }
          ],
